From: Markus Bertheau <mbertheau@localhost>
Subject: Fill hardware cursors from DRM dumb buffers

virtio-gpu's cursor overlay only uploads CPU-written dumb buffers.
GLES into a GBM SCANOUT|RENDERING buffer still KMS-commits, so
software compositing is skipped and the pointer is invisible.

Also ignore unknown libinput switch types and keep strchr's const
so the package builds with current libinput and gcc 15.

